<p>Thank you &#8212; I really appreciate it!</p>
<p>Dialogue is something that comes pretty naturally to me; probably because I enjoy listening to people and breaking apart how they communicate. I've been experimenting with trying to increase the verisimilitude of my dialogue (because yeah, dialogue <em>definitely</em> doesn't sound anything like how we write it, or portray it on TV &#8212; it's full of odd pauses, interruptions, repetitions, interjected affirmations, etc) while trying not to sacrifice its readability or flow. I think real dialogue is actually pretty boring to read (sometimes bordering on incomprehensible!) but there's a happy medium between 'real' and 'fictitious' that I'm trying to tap into, particularly recently &#8212; I'm very glad to hear that it's working!</p>
<p>(Also, thanks for the fix/noticing that &#8212; the PUA is meant to say <em>Cicadetta montana</em>, not <em>Cicada montana</em> &#8212; fixed!)</p>

