<p>+1</p>
<p>This is the third time I'm reading this, and the third time I'm commenting on it, and the third time I'm upvoting it. I swear if I see it again, I'm downvoting it. Anyway, as I read through this (for the third time) I will make comments.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>(I/O-SILVER)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That really is a super clever name for a bot.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the most prominent of which is a fixation on achieving material success via the application of rituals associated with the Cétlaidí, or &quot;Singers&quot; (a Druidic cult active in Ireland between the 15th and 19th centuries).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>By bringing these crosslinks up so soon, you are playing your had a bit early here. However, I do feel that this is unique enough to stand on its own, and unique enough In-Unvierse to be its own separate phenomenon.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Maybe you've heard that the Bible only nourishes the spirit; that God provides only for our immortal souls. Well, my friends, I am here to tell you that this is simply not true.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As before, your Bible-thumper passages are SPOT ON. I actually read these in Peter Popoff's voice, and it works quite well.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You are His children. You are His champions.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>During one iteration, I believe you had it singular. &quot;You are His child. You are His Champion.&quot; As someone who was born as raised religious (but no longer) that really resonated with me. For the briefest moment, I thought to myself, &quot;This is speaking to me. I -am- his Champion.&quot; Having it plural dulls the impact for me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Each of you, take one, and hold it in your left hand. Yes. The left hand, not the right. Your left.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Bits like this make it feel so very real. Like it's really a transcript of some guy in front of a crowd, giving directions.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;…lamb is slaughtered to feed the lion. The Son is slaughtered to feed…&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This little passage stands out to me as being especially disturbing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>chittering</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, did you decide on a head-canon where this fits with the Kafka Garage after all?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Ladders exist so you can climb them. That's what ladders are for, people! [&#8230;] If you're not going for the top of that ladder, then this video isn't for you. Bye! Sorry to have wasted your time. Successful people don't deal with losers. Only keep watching if you want to achieve complete mastery over your life.&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, you really hit the nail on the head with this transcript. This sounds EXACTLY like one of those motivational talks for dumb people.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>They'll start coughing up cicadas and shit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>While I like how you change up the format with everything by making this two people conversing, this one line really pulls me out of it. Unless this is for an anamolous community, someone hearing that is going to wonder just what the hell is going on here. You might make it something like, &quot;It'll start attracting cicadas to her. They'll show up in her clothing, in her dresser, in her bed&#8230; one time I heard of one trying to crawl up&#8230;&quot;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>All in all, an excellent piece to be proud of. I hope you are able to continue so the community can be enriched by more of your work!</p>

